%% Agentless VMware replication lifecycle in Azure Migrate - the states a server passes through and where it falls back
%% Source: Microsoft Learn "Migrate VMware VMs agentless" (execution stage and status, test migration, complete migration) and "Support for VMware vSphere migration in Azure Migrate" (limits, ports)
stateDiagram-v2
  direction TB
  [*] --> Discovered

  state "Discovered by the appliance" as Discovered
  state "Assessed - readiness, sizing, cost" as Assessed
  Discovered --> Assessed : discovery and assessment traffic goes to the project private endpoint
  Assessed --> EnableReplication : Execute then Migration then Start execution

  state "Enable replication" as EnableReplication
  note right of EnableReplication
    Target settings pick the cache storage account.
    After the first replication of a VM the target
    region and the storage account can no longer be changed.
    Portal selects at most 10 VMs per batch.
  end note

  state Preparation {
    [*] --> InitialReplication
    state "Initial replication - VMware snapshot, seed disks written to Azure" as InitialReplication
    InitialReplication --> [*] : initial replication complete
  }
  EnableReplication --> Preparation

  state Testing {
    [*] --> DeltaReplication
    state "Delta replication - changed blocks only, VM is ready to migrate" as DeltaReplication
    state "Test migration - Azure VM built on a non-production VNet" as TestMigration
    DeltaReplication --> TestMigration : Start test migration
    TestMigration --> DeltaReplication : Clean up test migration
    note right of TestMigration
      The source VM stays running and keeps replicating.
      Run this at least once for every machine.
    end note
  }
  Preparation --> Testing : initial replication finished

  state Completion {
    [*] --> Cutover
    state "Migrate - shut down the source VM, on-demand final replication, no data loss" as Cutover
    state "Migrated - Azure VM running, replication state still held" as Migrated
    Cutover --> Migrated
    Migrated --> [*] : Complete migration stops replication and cleans replication state
  }
  Testing --> Completion : test validated or testing skipped
  Completion --> Decommissioned

  state "Decommissioned - source removed from vCenter inventory and local backups" as Decommissioned
  Decommissioned --> [*]

  Preparation --> CycleReset : Azure connectivity or appliance services down for more than 90 minutes
  Testing --> CycleReset : Azure connectivity or appliance services down for more than 90 minutes
  state "Replication cycle resets from 0 percent" as CycleReset
  CycleReset --> Preparation : appliance recovers and initial replication restarts

  Preparation --> Stopped : Stop replication
  Testing --> Stopped : Stop replication
  state "Stopped - replication state discarded, seed disks removed" as Stopped
  Stopped --> EnableReplication : re-enable, which repeats the full initial replication

  note left of Preparation
    Execution stage is Preparation, Testing or Completion.
    Execution status is In progress, In error, Action pending or Completed.
    Up to 300 VMs replicate at once per vCenter with one appliance,
    up to 500 with a scale-out appliance.
    Appliance outbound 443 to Azure, inbound 443 on vCenter,
    inbound TCP 902 on each ESXi host.
  end note
